  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "decode_R13_R2000",
    "file": "libredwg/src/decode.c",
    "description": "`decode_R13_R2000` contains a hard `assert(dat->byte == 0xb)` at entry (line ~322) that assumes a fully valid parser state after version detection. For malformed/truncated DWG input, this invariant is not guaranteed, so the parser aborts via `__assert_fail` instead of returning a normal decode error. This is a reachable assertion-based DoS, caused by missing runtime validation/error handling before relying on internal state.",
    "conditions": "Via `llvmfuzz`, any input beginning with `AC` is routed to `dwg_decode`, which selects the R13-R2000 path and calls `decode_R13_R2000`. A crafted short/invalid DWG header (as in the PoC) causes `dat->byte` to differ from expected `0xb` when entering `decode_R13_R2000`, triggering the assert and process abort. Trigger requires AC-prefixed data that passes initial version dispatch but leaves parser offset/state inconsistent with the asserted invariant."
  },
